AEGNUX
------

NuxFX is based on AEGNUX (https://github.com/relativemodder/aegnux), which is licensed
under the GNU General Public License, version 3. AEGNUX is inspired by AeNux by cutefish
(https://github.com/cutefishaep/AeNux). NuxFX keeps the folder layout and the naming of
AEGNUX (~/.local/share/aegnux, AEGNUX_* settings) and is distributed under the GNU General
Public License as well (version 3 or later, see above).

Prebuilt Mesa packages (release assets)
---------------------------------------

The releases of this project carry two packages with binaries built from Mesa 25.2.8 and
the patches in patches/ (scripts/package_prebuilt.sh; prebuilt/manifest.txt lists them):
the Vulkan driver libvulkan_dzn.so, and Mesa's EGL and Direct3D 12 OpenGL driver
(libEGL, libGLESv2, libgallium). They are not part of the source tree. Each package holds
the Mesa license texts (LICENSE-Mesa.rst and licenses/), the license of DirectX-Headers
(Microsoft, MIT), which Meson links into both libraries, and SOURCE.txt with the Mesa
version, the hash of the patch series and the checksum of every patch. The corresponding
source is the Mesa 25.2.8 release tarball plus the patches of this repository.

Other components
----------------

NuxFX does not contain Wine, the Wine TkG runner, DXVK, vkd3d-proton, nvidia-libs, the
Mesa release tarball or any Adobe software (the Mesa packages above are built from the
tarball and the patches). These keep their own licenses. Their upstream projects:

- Wine TkG:      https://github.com/Frogging-Family/wine-tkg-git
- DXVK:          https://github.com/doitsujin/dxvk
- vkd3d-proton:  https://github.com/HansKristian-Work/vkd3d-proton
- nvidia-libs:   https://github.com/SveSop/nvidia-libs
- Mesa:          https://mesa3d.org

